senses.gloss:
पर्णसि, इस्, m. (said to be fr. rt. पॄ), a house
upon or by the water; a summer-house (?); a lotus;
a vegetable; adorning, decoration, toilet.

पर्णाश or पर्णास, अस्, m. a species of plant, a
kind of basil with small leaves, Ocymum Sanctum;
(आ), f., N. of various rivers; [cf. पूर्णाशा.]

पर्णिन्, ई, इनी, इ, winged, plumed; leafy, having
leaves, leaved; (ई), m. a tree; Butea Frondosa;
(इनी), f. a species of plant; N. of an Apsaras.
